---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { ADS_MODE } from '../data/ads';
---

<PageLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.brand}`}
  description={`How ${SITE.brand} handles your data: files are processed locally in your browser and never uploaded. Details on cookies, ads and hosting.`}
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  path="/privacy-policy"
  updated="[TODO: date]"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what happens to your data when you use {SITE.brand}
    (<span>{SITE.domain}</span>). The short version: the files you open in our tools stay on
    your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Files you process</h2>
  <p>
    All tools on this site run in your web browser. When you select a PDF, an image or a text
    file, it is read and processed locally on your device using code that loaded with the
    page. Your files are <strong>not uploaded</strong> to our servers or to any third party,
    and we cannot see, store or recover them. The same applies to text you type into the word
    counter, character counter and QR code generator, and to numbers you enter into the
    calculators.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some tools may save your most recent input in your browser's own storage (for example, an
    unsent draft in the word counter) so it is still there when you come back. This data stays
    on your device, and you can clear it from the tool or from your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by a hosting provider
    <span class="placeholder">[TODO: confirm provider, e.g. Cloudflare Pages]</span>. Like any
    website, the provider receives standard technical information when your browser requests a
    page, such as your IP address, browser type and the page requested. This is needed to
    deliver the site and protect it from abuse. It does not include the files you process in
    the tools.
  </p>

  {
    ADS_MODE === 'live' ? (
      <>
        <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site shows ads provided by Google AdSense to keep the tools free. Google and its partners
          may use cookies and similar technologies to show ads, measure them and prevent fraud. Ads are
          never given access to the files, text or numbers you use in our tools; those stay in your
          browser.
        </p>
        <p>
          Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for
          consent through Google's consent message (a Google-certified consent management platform)
          before personalized ads are shown. You can change your choice at any time with the
          "Privacy settings" link at the bottom of every page.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="placeholder">[TODO: your final wording: which ad partners, legal basis where required, how long choices are kept, and your contact for privacy requests.]</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          Read{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
            How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services
          </a>
          , and how Google uses cookies in{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">
            advertising
          </a>
          . You can manage personalized ads in{' '}
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">
            Google Ad Settings
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The site does not currently use advertising or analytics cookies. We plan to show ads in
          the future through Google AdSense. When that happens, Google and its partners may use
          cookies to serve ads based on your visits to this and other websites, and we will update
          this policy and ask for your consent where the law requires it. You can read how Google
          uses information from sites that use its services in{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
            Google's partner sites policy
          </a>
          , and how it uses cookies in advertising in{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">
            Google's advertising policy
          </a>
          . You can manage personalized ads in{' '}
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">
            Google Ad Settings
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you write, and we use it only
    to reply. We do not sell or share it.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a general-audience tool site and does not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    <span class="placeholder">[TODO: add the site operator's name and country if required in your jurisdiction]</span>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
